# Test: the daemon narrows the licence document to one work with `| name`.
# QUESTION: does a running daemon answer `show thanks licence | name
# github.com/miekg/dns` over SSH with that one work's copyright and licence
# text and no other work's, and refuse a name no carried work has, naming
# `show thanks list` as the way to see the names?
# A unit test cannot decide it: the operation is partitioned off the line by
# the daemon dispatcher (Dispatcher.dispatchLine, DispatchLine.DeclaredOperations)
# and must reach the local-data handler through the bridge
# (local_bridge.go localDataHandler, command.AnswerRemote), a path only a real
# daemon and a real SSH client exercise. This file is the proof of the spec's
# assumption A-4.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-thanks-third-party-credits AC-8 (Wiring row
#   `show thanks licence | name <work>` through the daemon).
# PREVENTS: a declared operation dropped on the daemon route, which would
#   answer every text, and an unknown name answered with an empty document.
#
# `show thanks licence` is only the daemon path of the local registration
# `thanks licence`, so `ze cli -c` sends these lines to the daemon over SSH.
# The copyright line is copied from vendor/github.com/miekg/dns/LICENSE.
#
# EXIT CODE and STREAM of the refusal: `ze cli -c` exits 1 and prints the
# operator error on stderr, as the draft run of 2026-11-20 observed.
#
# The text rendering carries no pipe metadata, so this file proves the
# narrowing by its content: the one work's heading, copyright line and source,
# and the absence of another work's text. The pipe step itself is asserted by
# the local-data coverage walk (test/ui/pipe-local-command.ci, runThanksCommands).

option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=thanks-daemon.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start thanks-daemon.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
reject=stderr:contains=panic

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "show thanks licence | name github.com/miekg/dns":exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=github\.com/miekg/dns v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+, LICENSE
expect=stdout:contains=Copyright (c) 2009, The Go Authors. Extensions copyright (c) 2011, Miek Gieben.
expect=stdout:contains=https://github.com/miekg/dns
reject=stdout:contains=golang.org/x/sys
reject=stdout:contains=Apache License

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "show thanks licence | name example.invalid/not-carried":exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=no work named example.invalid/not-carried is carried by this binary
expect=stderr:contains=show thanks list

cmd=stop:seq=5:name=daemon:signal=term
